# Irreducibility of the universal divisor over an affine chart

Let `A` be a Noetherian domain and let `f₁, …, f_r ∈ A` with `f₁ ≠ 0`. The *universal linear
form* of `f` is `x₁f₁ + ⋯ + x_rf_r ∈ A[x₁, …, x_r]`. If every irreducible component of the
common zero locus `V(f₁, …, f_r) ⊂ Spec A` has codimension at least two, then the zero locus of
the universal linear form is irreducible.

This is the local step in the proof of [Stacks, Tag 0G4F]: over an affine open `U = Spec A` of
`X` trivializing the invertible module, the universal divisor `H_univ ⊂ 𝔸^r_k ×_k X` of the
Bertini situation [Stacks, Tag 0G47] is cut out of `𝔸^r_U` by the universal linear form of the
elements `fᵢ ∈ A` corresponding to the sections `ψ(vᵢ)`, and the hypothesis on `V(f₁, …, f_r)`
is hypothesis (4) of Tag 0G4F read on the chart.

## Main results

* `PrimeSpectrum.isIrreducible_zeroLocus_image`: an isomorphism of rings carries an irreducible
  zero locus to an irreducible zero locus.
* `Algebra.isPrime_span_universalLinearForm`: over a domain in which `f₁` is invertible the
  universal linear form generates a prime ideal — eliminating `x₁` identifies the quotient with
  a polynomial ring in `x₂, …, x_r`.
* `Algebra.comap_C_eq_bot_of_mem_minimalPrimes`: every minimal prime over the universal linear
  form meets `A` only in zero.
* `Algebra.radical_span_universalLinearForm`: the radical of the ideal generated by the
  universal linear form is the contraction of the prime it generates over the fraction field.
* `Algebra.isIrreducible_zeroLocus_universalLinearForm`: the universal divisor over the chart is
  irreducible.
* `Algebra.isIrreducible_zeroLocus_linearForm`: the same with the parameters indexed by an
  arbitrary finite set, which is the form the parameter space of the Bertini situation supplies.
* `Algebra.isIrreducible_zeroLocus_linearForm_of_isPrime_nilradical`: the same for a Noetherian
  ring whose nilradical is prime — that is, with `Spec A` irreducible but `A` not assumed
  reduced. This is the reduction step of the source, carried out on the chart ring.

## The four stages, and where the tag is closed

Tag 0G4F concludes that `H_v` is geometrically irreducible over `k'` for general
`v ∈ V ⊗_k k'`. Its proof has four stages: the irreducibility of the universal divisor on an
affine chart, by the dimension count carried out here; the passage from the charts to `H_univ`;
the computation, via Tag 054Q, of the generic fibre of `H_univ → 𝔸^r_k` as the field extension
`K(x₂, …, x_r)/k(x₂, …, x_r, ξ)` obtained by eliminating `x₁`; and the passage from the generic
member to general members by Tag 0559.

All four stages are proved and **the tag is closed**: the unqualified `@[stacks 0G4F]` sits on
`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.Hypotheses.forGeneral_geometricallyIrreducible` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.BertiniUniversalDivisorGenericFibre`, which
deduces the conclusion of the tag from its hypotheses (1)–(4) alone. The registrations in this
module and elsewhere in the development stay qualified: each of them covers one stage, and the
statements here are about the chart ring rather than about `H_v`.

### The first two stages, from the tag's own hypotheses

The hypotheses (1)–(4) of the tag are formalized in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.BertiniHypotheses` as
`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.Hypotheses`, on the common zero locus
`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.commonZeroSet` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.BertiniCommonZeroSet`; see that module's
docstring for the two points at which a faithful rendering forced a choice. The derivations the
chart machinery consumes are
`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.Hypotheses.exists_not_isNilpotent_chartEquation` (hypothesis (3),
giving `f i₀` non-nilpotent on every chart) and
`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.Hypotheses.two_le_height_chartEquation` (hypothesis (4), giving
`2 ≤ Ideal.height` on the minimal primes of `(f₁, …, f_r)` in every chart ring), the latter
through the two bridges `PrimeSpectrum.codimension_irreducibleClosedsOfPrime` (codimension in
`Spec A` is the height of the prime, in
`StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Spectrum.Prime.CodimensionHeight`) and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.le_height_of_mem_minimalPrimes_of_isAffineOpen` (a codimension bound on
a scheme read on an affine open, in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Codimension.AffineOpenHeight`). Open-invariance of codimension is
not rebuilt: it is Tag 02I4, already in this library as
`TopologicalSpace.IrreducibleCloseds.coheight_restrictOpen`, and in Mathlib as
`Topology.IsOpenEmbedding.coheight_map`.

The second stage is proved in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.BertiniChartSupport`: the charts of `𝔸^r_X` over
the affine opens of `X` trivializing `L` carry the universal linear form as the local equation of
`H_univ` (`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.ideal_universalDivisor_chartOpen`), each chart piece of
the support of `H_univ` is therefore irreducible
(`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.isIrreducible_supportSet_inter_chart`), and the pieces glue to
`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.isIrreducible_supportSet_universalDivisor_of_directed`, whence
`H_univ` is an irreducible scheme by
`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.irreducibleSpace_universalDivisor_subscheme`. The trivializing
affine charts are `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.Chart`, they form a basis of the topology by
`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.exists_chart_le` and hence cover
(`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.iSup_chart_eq_top`) and refine intersections
(`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.exists_chart_le_inf`).

Assembling all of this,
`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.Hypotheses.isIrreducible_supportSet_universalDivisor` and
`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.Hypotheses.irreducibleSpace_universalDivisorScheme` deduce the
first two stages **from the tag's own hypotheses only**: neither carries a reducedness hypothesis
on `X`, and neither assumes local triviality of `L`.

* *Reducedness.* The source begins by replacing `X` by `X_red`. That replacement is made here one
  chart at a time instead: hypothesis (2) makes each chart's spectrum irreducible, hence the
  nilradical of each chart ring prime
  (`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.Hypotheses.isPrime_nilradical_chart`), and
  `Algebra.isIrreducible_zeroLocus_linearForm_of_isPrime_nilradical` runs the dimension count in
  the reduced quotient of the chart ring. The transports it needs — the spectrum, the heights and
  the minimal primes are unchanged by killing an ideal of nilpotents — are
  `StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Ideal.NilradicalQuotient`. No vocabulary for `X_red` is required, and
  the conclusion is about `X` itself, so nothing has to be transported back.
* *Local triviality of `L`.* That the affine opens trivializing `L` form a basis of the topology
  is now a theorem, `Stacks.Modules.exists_affineOpen_pullback_iso_unit_of_isInvertible` of
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleLocal.AffineBasis`: a trivializing open produced by
  Tag 0B8M is shrunk to an affine one inside any prescribed open, in the localized-site spelling,
  by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isoUnitOverOfHom`.

### The fourth stage

`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.forGeneral_geometricallyIrreducible_of_genericFibre`, which is
Tag 0559 applied to `H_univ → 𝔸^r_k`. Its one input is the hypothesis `hgen`: that the fibre of
`H_univ → 𝔸^r_k` over the generic point is geometrically irreducible. That is supplied by
`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.Hypotheses.geometricallyIrreducible_fiber_genericPoint`, the
third stage.

### The third stage at the level of schemes

The chart-level field-theoretic content is proved in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.BertiniChartFunctionField`: eliminating `x₁` from
the universal linear form over a chart on which the first section is invertible is
`Algebra.quotientSpanUniversalLinearFormEquiv`, and
`Algebra.isGeometricallyIrreducible_universalDivisorChart` is the resulting field extension
together with its geometric irreducibility, which is Tags 0G4D and 0G4E through
`Algebra.isGeometricallyIrreducible_adjoin_linearCombination_of_codimTwo`. The passage from there
to `hgen` has the following inputs available.

* **Available.** The ring of `H_univ` over a chart is `A[xᵢ]/(∑ᵢ xᵢfᵢ)`:
  `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.chartSubschemeΓEquiv`, the transport of Mathlib's
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeObjIso` through
  `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.chartMvPolynomialEquiv`.
* **Available.** The residue field `κ(η)` at the generic point of `𝔸^r_k` is a fraction field of
  `k[xᵢ : i ∈ ι]`, generated over `k` by the images of the coordinates:
  `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.isFractionRing_parameterBase` and
  `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.adjoin_range_coord_parameterBase_eq_top` of
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.BertiniParameterFunctionField`.
* **Available.** The generic fibre of a dominant morphism from an irreducible scheme is
  irreducible: `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.irreducibleSpace_fiber_of_denseRange` of
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.GenericFibre.IrreducibleOfDominant`. Note that
  `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.Hypotheses.irreducibleSpace_universalDivisorScheme` is an
  *input* to this and not the statement itself.
* **Available — and no reduced model of the generic fibre is needed.** Tag 054Q as formalized,
  `AlgebraicGeometry.geometricallyIrreducible_tfae_functionField`, asks only for an *irreducible*
  scheme and speaks of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.residueField` at a generic point, not of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.functionField` of an integral one. It therefore applies to the generic
  fibre of `H_univ → 𝔸^r_k` as it stands, and the source's replacement of `X` by `X_red` is not
  needed here either. (A transport of `GeometricallyIrreducible` along a reduction `Z_red → Z` does
  exist, as `AlgebraicGeometry.geometricallyIrreducible_comp_iff_of_universalHomeomorphism` of
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.GenericFibre.UniversalHomeomorphismTransport`
  together with the instance `AlgebraicGeometry.universalHomeomorphism_nilradical_subschemeι`;
  it is not needed.)
* **Available.** The residue field at the generic point of the generic fibre is the residue field
  of the source at its generic point: `AlgebraicGeometry.genericFiberResidueFieldMap`, an
  isomorphism of `κ(η)`-algebras by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.residueFieldMapOfEq_comp_genericFiberResidueFieldMap`. Those now ask only for
  an irreducible source. Assembled with Tag 054Q they give
  `AlgebraicGeometry.geometricallyIrreducible_fiber_genericPoint_iff_residueField_of_isAffine` of
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.MoreMorphisms.GenericFibre.GenericFibreResidueFieldCriterion`:
  for `f : X ⟶ Y` with `X` irreducible, `Y` integral and affine and `f` carrying the generic point
  of `X` to that of `Y`, the generic fibre is geometrically irreducible over `κ(η)` exactly when
  `κ(ξ)` is, for `ξ` the generic point of `X`. **This turns `hgen` into a statement about
  `H_univ` itself**, with neither a fibre nor a reduction left in it.
* **Proved: the dominance of `H_univ → 𝔸^r_k`.**
  `Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.Hypotheses.isDominant_universalFamily` of
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.BertiniUniversalFamilyDominance`, from the
  tag's own hypotheses. On a chart it is
  `Algebra.algebraicIndependent_universalDivisorChartMap_X`: the images of the parameters in a
  fraction field of the chart ring are algebraically independent over `k`, so `k[xⱼ]` injects
  into it. That is Tag 0G4E once more, through
  `Algebra.algebraicIndependent_linearCombination_of_codimTwo`; it is where the codimension-two
  hypothesis enters, and without it dominance can genuinely fail. The passage to the scheme is
  `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.Fibres.BertiniUniversalFamilyChart`: the part of
  `H_univ` over a chart is an affine open
  (`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.isAffineOpen_chartDivisorOpen`, the range of the matching
  member of Mathlib's `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.subschemeCover`), the ring map of
  the family there is the structural `k[xⱼ] → Γ(U, ⊤)[xⱼ]/(∑ⱼ xⱼfⱼ)`
  (`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.chartDivisorParameterMap_parameterBaseΓEquiv`, by
  `AlgebraicGeometry.AffineSpace.map_appTop_coord` on the coordinates and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.AffineSpace.map_appTop_over_appTop` on the constants), composing it with
  the reduction of the coefficients and the inclusion into `Ω` gives evaluation at the images of
  the parameters, hence injectivity
  (`Stacks.Bertini.FamilyDivisors.injective_chartDivisorParameterMap`), and a morphism with
  quasi-compact source and affine target injective on global sections is dominant
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.isDominant_of_of_appTop_injective`, then
  `AlgebraicGeometry.IsDominant.of_comp` to cancel the open immersion). The `Ω` used there is
  `FractionRing (reducedChartDivisorRing c)`, which is a domain by the item below.
* **Available: the distinguished vectors need not be basis vectors.** Both chart statements hold
  for an *arbitrary invertible `k`-linear change of the parameters*, and for parameters indexed
